# 🎨 CSS Selectors Practice Assignment

This assignment is designed to strengthen the fundamentals of **CSS Selectors**, **Pseudo Classes**, **Pseudo Elements**, and **CSS Specificity**. It covers the most commonly used selectors in web development.

---

# 📚 Topics Covered

- ID Selector (`#`)
- Universal Selector (`*`)
- Group Selector (`,`)
- Class Selector (`.`)
- Descendant Selector (` `)
- Pseudo Class (`:hover`)
- Structural Pseudo Class (`:nth-of-type()`)
- Pseudo Element (`::first-letter`)
- Adjacent Sibling Selector (`+`)
- Checkbox State Selector (`:checked`)
- CSS Specificity

---

# 📝 Practice Questions

## ✅ Q1. ID Selector

**Task**

Give the `h1` heading a unique id `"mainTopic"` and set its color to **blue** using the **ID Selector**.

### Concept

- ID Selector
- Unique Element Styling

### Selector Used

```css
#mainTopic
```

---

## ✅ Q2. Universal Selector

**Task**

Align all the text on the page to the center using the **Universal Selector**.

### Concept

- Universal Selector

### Selector Used

```css
*
```

---

## ✅ Q3. Group Selector

**Task**

Change the font family of all heading tags (`h1` to `h6`) to **Georgia**.

### Concept

- Group Selector

### Selector Used

```css
h1,
h2,
h3,
h4,
h5,
h6
```

---

## ✅ Q4. Class Selector

**Task**

Change all paragraph text color to **white** and background color to **cornflowerblue** **without using the element selector (`p`)**.

### Concept

- Class Selector

### Selector Used

```css
.para
```

---

## ✅ Q5. Descendant Selector

**Task**

Select all buttons inside a `<div>` and change:

- Background Color → Purple
- Text Color → Azure

### Concept

- Descendant Selector

### Selector Used

```css
div button
```

---

## ✅ Q6. Hover Pseudo Class

**Task**

Change the button background color to **yellow** and text color to **blue** when the mouse hovers over it.

### Concept

- Pseudo Class

### Selector Used

```css
button:hover
```

---

## ✅ Q7. Structural Pseudo Class

**Task**

Change the color of every **odd-numbered paragraph** to **yellow**.

### Concept

- `:nth-of-type()`

### Selector Used

```css
p:nth-of-type(odd)
```

---

## ✅ Q8. Pseudo Element

**Task**

Change the **first letter** of the `h1` heading to **red**.

### Concept

- Pseudo Element

### Selector Used

```css
h1::first-letter
```

---

## ✅ Q9. Adjacent Sibling Selector

**Task**

When the checkbox is checked, change the corresponding label color to **dark green**.

### Concept

- Adjacent Sibling Selector
- `:checked`

### Selector Used

```css
input[type="checkbox"]:checked + label
```

---

## ✅ Q10. CSS Specificity

**Task**

Arrange the following selectors from **least specific** to **most specific**.

### Given Selectors

```css
h1
.main
div .main
#mainContent
```

### Correct Order

```text
h1
↓
.main
↓
div .main
↓
#mainContent
```

### Specificity Scores

| Selector | Specificity |
|----------|-------------|
| `h1` | (0,0,0,1) |
| `.main` | (0,0,1,0) |
| `div .main` | (0,0,1,1) |
| `#mainContent` | (0,1,0,0) |

---

# 🎯 CSS Selectors Learned

| Selector | Example |
|----------|---------|
| Universal Selector | `*` |
| Element Selector | `p` |
| ID Selector | `#mainTopic` |
| Class Selector | `.para` |
| Group Selector | `h1, h2, h3` |
| Descendant Selector | `div button` |
| Adjacent Sibling Selector | `input + label` |
| Pseudo Class | `:hover` |
| Structural Pseudo Class | `:nth-of-type(odd)` |
| Pseudo Element | `::first-letter` |

---

# 🧠 Key Takeaways

- ID Selectors have higher specificity than Class Selectors.
- Class Selectors have higher specificity than Element Selectors.
- Universal Selector selects every element.
- Descendant Selectors target nested elements.
- Pseudo Classes represent an element's **state**.
- Pseudo Elements style **specific parts** of an element.
- CSS Specificity determines which rule is applied when multiple rules target the same element.

---

